Package: erhai-firmware
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Description: OnePlus Pad 2 Pro (erhai) firmware closure
 The firmware this unit's mainline drivers ask for by name and the
 distribution does not ship under that name: the NT36536 touch controller's
 application firmware, the Adreno 830 SQE/GMU/AQE microcode and its zap
 shader, the WCN7860 Wi-Fi and Bluetooth images, the ADSP/CDSP PIL sets, and
 the board's AW88261 amplifier profiles prepared for audio bring-up.
 .
 This kernel is built without CONFIG_FW_LOADER_COMPRESS, so the zstd-suffixed
 copies in linux-firmware are unreadable to it even where the same file
 exists; every path here is a plain file under a name no other package owns,
 so nothing is diverted and nothing is overwritten.
 .
 The binaries live in the project's packaging/firmware tree, taken unmodified
 from this unit's stock ROM images and from pinned upstream archives, and each
 one is checked against the sha256 and size recorded in
 packaging/firmware-manifest.json before it is packed. They are proprietary
 Qualcomm, OnePlus and Awinic binaries under their own terms, not the packaging's
 GPL-2.0-only; packaging/firmware/README.md says where each came from.
